        "question": "My customer wants to postpone her honeymoon trip by a month. Is that possible and what does it cost?",
        "text": "Date changes on vacation packages are allowed up to 21 days before departure, subject to availability [changes#date-changes]. The agency charges a USD 40 change fee per booking, plus any price difference from hotels or airlines [changes#date-changes]. If the change falls inside 21 days before departure, it is treated as a cancellation followed by a new booking [changes#date-changes]. Advisors can process date changes, but waiving the fee requires supervisor approval [changes#who-can-approve-changes].",
